```diff
{{diff}}
```

Look for: injection (SQL / command / template), broken authentication or authorization, secrets or credentials in code,
unsafe deserialization, path traversal, SSRF, XSS, insecure crypto or randomness, missing input validation at trust
boundaries, sensitive data in logs, and anything AI_SECURITY.md forbids. Report only real problems in the changed code.
Severity: critical / high = exploitable or a rule of AI_SECURITY.md broken; medium / low = hardening.

Reply with ONLY one fenced `json` block:
{"verdict": "pass" | "fail", "findings": [{"severity": "critical|high|medium|low", "file": "<path>", "line": <number or 0>, "issue": "<what is wrong>", "fix": "<how to fix it>"}]}
The verdict is "fail" when any finding is critical or high, else "pass".

